## WHY (the three routes; MEASURED-BY-DRAFTER by reading source at `30b957b4`, plus one run of a pure function)
1. **`GET /api/models` throws on EVERY request, not only on an empty store.** The handler (`backend/server.js:19083`) maps `getEnabledModels()` with `([key, model]) =>` (`:19088`) and `key === MODEL_CONFIG.activeModel` (`:19094`), but `getEnabledModels` (`model-config.js:299`) returns an array of OBJECTS `{ key, name, description, type, requirements }`. Run at drafting under plain node: `Array.isArray(e[0])` false, `e.map(([key, model]) => key)` throws `TypeError: object is not iterable`; control: the same destructure over `[["a",{}]]` returns `a`. The sibling `POST /api/models/switch` already reads the objects (`:16247-16260`, comment "enabledModels returns objects with key, name, ..."). No page calls `GET /api/models` (`static/`, 0 hits for the path; control: the file `backend/server.js` has 4). The path is in `setupOnlyPaths` (`:2200`), public during the setup window.
2. **`POST /api/settings/agent` (`:20385`) and `POST /api/settings/business-hours` (`:20665`) destructure `req.body` and write key by key**, with `.toString()` on the last value (`:20391`, `:20392`, `:20675`). Express is `^5.1.0` (`package.json`), so `req.body` may be `undefined` on a request with no body (UNMEASURED: you measure it). An empty request: the agent route writes `agent_response_style` and `agent_language` as `undefined` (JSON.stringify drops the key; `setSetting` still stamps `<key>_updated_at`, `backend/jsonStorage.js:3434-3435`) and then answers 500; the business-hours route does the same for six keys. That is a partial write with no reason given (the rule is C-15: a bad request fails with a reason and changes nothing).
3. **The only real caller of business-hours is the Settings page** (`static/js/settings.js:2803-2824`): it posts `weekdayStart, weekdayEnd, saturdayStart, saturdayEnd, excludeSunday` and adds `sundayStart, sundayEnd` ONLY when `excludeSunday` is false (`:2813-2816`), from `<input type="time">` fields (`static/settings.html:539-578`) that can be cleared to `''`. The default is Sunday excluded, so **the page's own body has no Sunday pair**. A validator that demands all seven fields would refuse the page's default save. The page also ignores the response status (`:2825-2830` alerts "saved" on any answer): out of scope (`static/**` is lane F1's); report it as a finding.
4. The agent form was removed by the product owner's 2026-09-26 ruling (CLARIFICATIONS C-166: the five preferences are read by nothing); the routes stayed (RD-691). Callers of the agent POST left: the two probe tests above, both with a complete, correctly typed five-field body (`responseStyle: 'concise', language: 'en', useEmojis: false, useMarkdown: true, agentRole: '...'`), which must stay 200.

## THE DESIGN (decided at source by the drafter; every omission needs your written justification)
1. **Validate first, write nothing on a refusal, keep the success path byte-identical.** Two small module-level functions in `backend/server.js`, placed directly above their routes, each returning the list of invalid field names (a fixed set of names, never user text, so a 400 body reflects no request value). The handler answers `400` with `{ success: false, error: 'Invalid agent settings: <names>', invalid: [<names>] }` (business hours: `'Invalid business hours: <names>'`) BEFORE the first `setSetting`; on success the same `setSetting` calls in the same order with the same `.toString()` values as today, so the stored file is identical for every valid body.
2. **Agent rule** (the five fields the removed form posted): the body must be a plain object (not `undefined`, `null`, an array or a string: all five names are then invalid); `responseStyle`, `language`, `agentRole` must be strings (empty allowed: the form allowed an empty role); `useEmojis`, `useMarkdown` must be a boolean or the exact string `'true'` or `'false'` (what `.toString()` accepts today and what is stored).
3. **Business-hours rule:** same plain-object test; `weekdayStart, weekdayEnd, saturdayStart, saturdayEnd` required, each a string that is `''` (the page can send a blank; today it stores it and the report falls back to its default) or matches the literal `/^([01][0-9]|2[0-3]):[0-5][0-9]$/` (anchored, fixed length, no nested quantifier: no ReDoS shape); `excludeSunday` required, a boolean or `'true'`/`'false'`; `sundayStart`/`sundayEnd` **optional when `excludeSunday` is true** (the page omits them; keep the two `setSetting(..., undefined)` calls exactly as today so the stored result is unchanged) and **required, valid, when `excludeSunday` is false** (the page always sends them then); when present they follow the same time rule. No ordering rule (start before end): not asked, and an overnight window is plausible.
4. **`GET /api/models`:** map the objects, `id: m.key`, `active: m.key === MODEL_CONFIG.activeModel`, keep the `memoryUsage`/`performance` keys (undefined, omitted from the JSON: they came from the removed Ollama provider; record it as a finding, do not remove them). The answer shape (`success`, `activeModel`, `availableModels`) stays. Do not touch `model-config.js` (outside this lane) and do not touch `GET /api/models/active`.
5. **No new role gate.** This kit adds no `requireAdminFor`-family call and no `role === 'admin'` test anywhere (the handler-span scan `__tests__/rd978-handler-span-scan.test.js` searches each handler's span for those tokens, and a token in a comment inside a span is a hit: keep the validation functions OUTSIDE the handlers and their comments free of those words). Who may call the routes is RD-958's, not yours; **RD-958's branch `b1480/nexusai-s-viewer-write-gates` (unmerged, 45 behind main) pins this route's admin status at `500`** (`__tests__/rd958-viewer-write-gates.test.js:37`, `['POST', '/api/settings/business-hours', 500]`, and the same in `rd958-write-gate-path-variants.test.js`); when this kit lands first, that branch's seat owns changing the pin to 400. Say so in READY (owed to that branch, not done by you).
6. **The inventory.** `docs/role-capabilities.json` records the status of ONE request per route per mode, with an empty `{}` body. After this fix the rows `GET /api/models`, `POST /api/settings/agent`, `POST /api/settings/business-hours` change (PREDICTED: viewer, administrator and open `500` to `200`, `400`, `400`; anonymous stays `401`; the `capability` sentences and `docs/ROLE-CAPABILITIES.md` follow). Regenerate with the tool from a **non-dot tree** (a path under `.tools/` fails `__tests__/rd438-dot-segment-gate.test.js`); never edit either file by hand (the JSON's own `_why`). Commit I carries both files and nothing else.
7. **Not done, said so in READY:** RD-691, RD-974, RD-975; every `static/` file; `model-config.js`; `backend/services/capabilities.js` and `scripts/role-capability-inventory.js` (read only); any role gate; the settings page's missing status check.

